    "https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/51375": {
      "title": "Chair of Medicine and Oncology",
      "description": "The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley Job Site | Chair of Medicine and Oncology Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Office Location The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley 1201 W. University Drive Human Resources MASS Building 2 nd Floor Edinburg, TX  78539 Edinburg: (956)665-2451 Brownsville: (956) 882-8205 Office hours: Monday-Friday 8:00a.m. - 5:00p.m. Staff Recruitment: careers@utrgv.edu School of Medicine Recruitment: SOMCareers@utrgv.edu Graduate Assistantships: assistantships@utrgv.edu Faculty Recruitment: College of Engineering & Computer Science: cecs@utrgv.edu Robert C. Vackar College of Business & Entrepreneurship: cobe@utrgv.edu College of Sciences Office of the Dean: cos@utrgv.edu College of Education and P-16 Integration: cep@utrgv.edu College of Fine Arts: cofa@utrgv.edu College of Liberal Arts: liberalarts@utrgv.edu Website: https://careers.utrgv.edu Chair of Medicine and Oncology Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: *Date of Birth *Social Security Number *Gender *Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. Security sensitive; All UTRGV employees are required to have a criminal background check (CBC). CBCs will be conducted for all candidates invited for an on-campus interview Posting Details Title Information Faculty Title Job Class Code FLSA Position Information Posting Number FRGV1996 Working Title Chair of Medicine and Oncology Number of Vacancies 1 Location Rio Grande Valley, Texas Division/Organization Division of Health Affairs Appointment Period for Non-Tenure Position 1 year Tenure Status Tenure Track FTE 1.0 Scope of Job The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley ( UTRGV ) School of Medicine invites applications for the position of Chair of the Department of Medicine and Oncology . This leader will set the department’s strategic vision, guide faculty development, and oversee all academic, clinical, and operational functions. The Chair reports directly to the Dean of the School of Medicine. Position Overview The Chair of Medicine and Oncology will lead the continued growth of an academic department dedicated to advancing cancer prevention, innovative research, and exceptional medical education. A central focus of the department is the development of a comprehensive academic oncology program addressing cancers prevalent in the Rio Grande Valley. The program integrates clinical services, translational research, clinical trials, and education within the Cancer and Surgery Center. The Chair is responsible for providing visionary leadership and ensuring excellence across all departmental missions, including: Clinical Leadership: Oversight of high quality patient care within all departmental clinical programs. Research Advancement: Support and growth of basic, translational, and clinical research initiatives, including clinical trials. Education: Integration of outstanding educational programs for medical students, residents, fellows, and other trainees. Faculty Development: Recruitment, mentorship, evaluation, and promotion of faculty; fostering a culture of wellness, collaboration, and professional growth. Administration: Financial oversight, budget planning, and resource allocation aligned with institutional priorities. Strategic Planning: Development and implementation of departmental strategies consistent with the School of Medicine’s mission. Representation: Serve as an ambassador for the department at local, regional, state, and national levels. Additional Responsibilities ( UTRGV School of Medicine Standard Expectations for Chairs) The Department Chair shall: Report directly to the Dean Ensure effective administration of the department Lead regular department meetings to communicate key updates, policies, and programmatic initiatives Recruit and recommend appointments of faculty, including community faculty Oversee implementation of all UTRGV and SOM policies applicable to the department Develop and submit the department’s annual budget, including compensation recommendations Manage departmental finances and space allocation Recommend faculty appointments, promotions, and tenure Organize the department to meet current and emerging needs of the School of Medicine Ensure faculty wellness, mentorship, career development, and performance evaluation Minimum Qualifications Eight (8) years of post clinical degree experience M.D. degree required; M.D./Ph.D. preferred Board certification in relevant specialty Eligibility for unrestricted Texas medical licensure Demonstrated excellence in clinical practice Administrative leadership experience at the departmental or institutional level Evidence of successful, independent clinical or translational research , with a history of grant or protocol funding Consistent contributions to education, training, and mentoring of trainees, faculty, or staff Progressive academic leadership experience; oncology focused leadership preferred Ability to thrive within an evolving hybrid medical school environment committed to education, research, and patient care Qualified for appointment at the rank of associate professor or full professor at an LCME accredited medical school. Discipline Specific Required Qualifications . Preferred Qualifications License or Certification Required? Yes Salary Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement It is the policy of The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley to promote and ensure equal employment opportunities for all individuals without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information or protected veteran status. In accordance with the requirements of Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, as amended, our University is committed to comply with all government requirements and ensures non-discrimination in its education programs and activities, including employment. We encourage women, minorities and differently abled persons to apply for employment positions of interest. Open Date 04/13/2026 Close Date Additional Information UTRGV is a distributed institution. As such and as assigned, the position may require presence at multiple locations throughout the Rio Grande Valley. Work is performed primarily in a general office environment. This position is security sensitive and thereby subject to the provisions of the Texas Education Code §51.215. The retirement plan for this position is Teacher Retirement System of Texas ( TRS ), subject to the position being at least 20 hours per week and at least 135 days in length. This position has the option to elect the Optional Retirement Program ( ORP ) instead of TRS , subject to the position being 40 hours per week and at least 135 days in length. Special Instructions to Applicants Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: Date of Birth Social Security Number Gender Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. Security sensitive; All UTRGV employees are required to have a criminal background check ( CBC ). CBCs will be conducted for all candidates invited for an on-campus interview Please Note Texas law requires faculty members whose primary language is not English to demonstrate proficiency in English as determined by a satisfactory paper-based test score of 500 (computer-based of 173 or internet-based of 61) on the Test of English as a Foreign Language ( TOEFL ) or a satisfactory test score of 6.0 on the International English Language Testing System ( IELTS ). Incomplete applications will not be considered. All positions are subject to budget approval. Quick Link https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50812 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Curriculum Vitae Optional Documents Resume Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 Certifications and Licenses Other Document List of 3 References Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Letter of Interest Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Teaching Statement State Licensure The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley UT System Employee Benefits UT System Fraud Reporting State