rande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. Posting Details Title Information Assistantship Title Graduate Assistant Job Class Code 10096 FLSA Exempt Minimum Qualifications 1.\tMust be admitted to a graduate degree program. 2.\tMust be in good academic standing 3.\tBe registered full-time for the respective semester – nine (9) semester credit hours during the fall semester, nine (9) semester credit hours during the spring semester, or three (3) semester credit hours during the summer session or be registered in the required number of semester credit hours to fulfill the only remaining requirements of the degree plan. Position Information Posting Number A1480 Working Title Graduate Assistant - Philosophy Location Edinburg, Texas College College of Liberal Arts Department College of Liberal Arts / Philosophy Division Provost - Academic Affairs FTE .25 Scope of Job The Graduate Assistant will provide programmatic, and research support to the Department of Philosophy’s Master of Science in Bioethics program. Responsibilities may include assisting with student recruitment and outreach activities, maintaining program records, supporting online and in-person events, conducting literature reviews and research related to bioethics topics, assisting with grant-related activities, preparing reports and program materials, and supporting faculty initiatives associated with the MS in Bioethics program. The Graduate Assistant will work collaboratively with faculty, staff, and students while contributing to the growth, promotion, and daily operations of the Bioethics program. Discipline Specific Required Qualifications Must be admitted to or enrolled in a graduate program. Demonstrated interest in bioethical issues, strong analytical and writing skills, and the ability to assist with academic and research activities related to the MS in Bioethics program Preferred Qualifications Coursework or experience in bioethics, healthcare ethics, research ethics, or philosophy of medicine. Experience with academic research, literature reviews, data management, or program support activities is preferred. Salary 2500.00 Number of Vacancies 1 Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement It is the policy of The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley to promote and ensure equal employment opportunities for all individuals without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information or protected veteran status. In accordance with the requirements of Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, as amended, our University is committed to comply with all government requirements and ensures non-discrimination in its education programs and activities, including employment. We encourage women, minorities and differently abled persons to apply for employment positions of interest. Open Date 08/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: Date of Birth Social Security Number Gender Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. Quick Link https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52269 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Teaching Philosophy Writing / Publication Sample Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts Reference Letter 1 List of 3 References The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley UT System Employee Benefits UT System Fraud Reporting State of Texas Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal Where the money goes To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
