      "title": "DIRECTOR, APEX ACCELERATOR",
      "description": "The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley Job Site | DIRECTOR, APEX ACCELERATOR Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Office Location The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley 1201 W. University Drive Human Resources MASS Building 2 nd Floor Edinburg, TX  78539 Edinburg: (956)665-2451 Brownsville: (956) 882-8205 Office hours: Monday-Friday 8:00a.m. - 5:00p.m. Staff Recruitment: careers@utrgv.edu School of Medicine Recruitment: SOMCareers@utrgv.edu Graduate Assistantships: assistantships@utrgv.edu Faculty Recruitment: College of Engineering & Computer Science: cecs@utrgv.edu Robert C. Vackar College of Business & Entrepreneurship: cobe@utrgv.edu College of Sciences Office of the Dean: cos@utrgv.edu College of Education and P-16 Integration: cep@utrgv.edu College of Fine Arts: cofa@utrgv.edu College of Liberal Arts: liberalarts@utrgv.edu Website: https://careers.utrgv.edu DIRECTOR, APEX ACCELERATOR Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: *Date of Birth *Gender *Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us at (956) 665-2451 and/or careers@utrgv.edu. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SRGV9094 Working Title DIRECTOR, APEX ACCELERATOR Number of Vacancies 1 Location Edinburg, Texas Department Business Development FTE 1.0 FLSA Exempt Scope of Job To manage and oversee the planning, organization and administration of the APEX Accelerator. Responsible for providing senior leadership skills and direction for the daily Operation of the APEX Accelerator Center. Description of Duties Provides leadership, direction, and oversight for the APEX Accelerator Center and its staff to achieve program objectives. Manages and prepares program grant application, budget, and required reports to maintain program compliance standards. Achieves established programmatic performance benchmarks and utilizes effective methods for program sustainability, growth, and status. Oversees and implements Center priorities and goals. Establishes and maintains resource partnerships. Manages client development and outreach activities. Interprets and markets program and services. Continuously evaluates program progress and quality. Researches potential funding sources. Establishes liaisons with local businesses, public officials, and economic development organizations to promote region. Coordinates with or presents to business clients, cities, counties, and school districts for consulting on projects. Develops appropriate internal or external reports as required for the project or program. Oversees the development and completion of research and survey designs. Develops and monitors assigned budgets to ensure compliance with prescribed regulations and procedures. Researches, writes, and develops proposals in support of Center’s mission and goals. Provides guidance and assistance in the research and development activities for the Center. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Received General direction from the assigned supervisor. Supervision Given Provides guidance to assigned staff. Required Education Bachelor’s degree in Business Administration or a related degree from an accredited University. Other discipline areas will be considered if past work experience was attained in administration, budget management or Project Management capacity related to functions being performed by this position. Preferred Education N/A Licenses/Certifications None. Required Experience Five (5) years progressively responsible professional experience related to the area, including experience in business, management, marketing, consulting, training or a related field. Experience in administration, budget management or Project Management and knowledge of grant proposal development process. Preferred Experience Supervisory experience. Equipment Experience with standard office equipment. Working Conditions Needs to be able to successfully perform all required duties. Usual office environment. Other Demonstrate effective written and verbal communication skills. Possess excellent interpersonal, influencing and collaboration skills. Some evening and /or weekend work and travel may be required. Ability to multi-task. Physical Capabilities N/A Employment Category Full-Time Minimum Salary Commensurate with Experience Posted Salary Commensurate with Experience Position Available Date 08/11/2026 Grant Funded Position Yes If Yes, Provide Grant Expiration Date Posting Detail Information EEO Statement It is the policy of The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley to promote and ensure equal employment opportunities for all individuals without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information or protected veteran status. In accordance with the requirements of Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, as amended, our University is committed to comply with all government requirements and ensures non-discrimination in its education programs and activities, including employment. We encourage women, minorities and differently abled persons to apply for employment positions of interest. Special Instructions to Applicants Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: Date of Birth Gender *Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us at (956) 665-2451 and/or careers@utrgv.edu. Additional Information UTRGV is a distributed location institution and working location is subject to change based on need. All UTRGV employees are required to have a criminal background check ( CBC ). Incomplete applications will not be considered. Substitutions to the above requirements must have prior approval from the VP of HR & Talent Development . Quick Link https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52158 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). * Are you a current UTRGV employee? Yes No * Are you now, or previously, employed by The University of Texas System or any of its institutions? Yes - I currently am employed by the UT System or its institutions Yes - I have previously been employed by the UT System