rtment as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. Posting Details Title Information Assistantship Title Graduate Research Assistant Job Class Code 10095 FLSA Exempt Minimum Qualifications 1.\tMust be admitted to a graduate degree program. 2.\tMust be in good academic standing 3.\tBe registered full-time for the respective semester – nine (9) semester credit hours during the fall semester, nine (9) semester credit hours during the spring semester, or three (3) semester credit hours during the summer session or be registered in the required number of semester credit hours to fulfill the only remaining requirements of the degree plan. Position Information Posting Number A1472 Working Title Graduate Research Assistant-Sustainable Agr and Rural Advncmt Location Edinburg, Texas College College of Sciences Department College of Sciences/ Sustainble Agr & Rural Advncmt Division Provost - Academic Affairs FTE 0.5 Scope of Job To assist staff, faculty, and Project Manager in the research needs of the Sustainable Agricultural and Rural Advancement Center ( SARA ) related projects/program’s purpose, activities and tasks. •Coordinates project programing to ensure that implementation and prescribed activities and tasks are carried out in accordance with specified objectives. •Must be able to coordinates the various activities of the projects/programs including outreach, trainings, technical assistance, and the creation of informational materials regarding cooperatives, businesses, and farm and ranch operations. •Helps coordinate long and short-term programs, including performing feasibility studies. •Drafts brochures, letters, and agendas. •Develops, plans, and creates social media communication and campaigns related to the project/programs. •May plan, develop, organize, and coordinate research and survey designs. Which can include data collection, processing, and analysis and evaluation of data. Dissemination of findings through publication of YouTube videos. •May assists others in writing and developing proposals for funding grants. •Attends meetings, conferences, and seminars related to the project’s/program’s mission and goals. •Helps supervise and organize seminars, conferences, and presentations. •Provides appropriate reports as required for the projects/programs to Project Manager. •May provide support in the coordination of general community and school gardens and related small-scale farm plots and farm site demonstration sites in an agricultural environment. Discipline Specific Required Qualifications • Ability to interact in a professional manner with faculty, staff, students and the public. • Excellent verbal and written communication skills. • Demonstrate interpersonal skills. • Independent decision making and problem-solving ability. • Must demonstrate effective project promotion skills, and the ability to develop and maintain strong working relations with internal and external agencies and entities. • Project/program may require ability to drive a car for local or distant travel for client consultation, training, meetings or small-scale farming on site demonstrations. • Must be able to bend, stoop, reach and lift for retrieving/maintaining files and for setting up multimedia equipment. Preferred Qualifications Business, Life Sciences, Communications, Public Affairs, Social Work, Sociology or other Agriculture-related field. Bilingual/Spanish proficiency preferred, but not required. Salary $1,500.00/month Number of Vacancies 3 Desired Start Date 09/01/2026 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement It is the policy of The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley to promote and ensure equal employment opportunities for all individuals without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information or protected veteran status. In accordance with the requirements of Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, as amended, our University is committed to comply with all government requirements and ensures non-discrimination in its education programs and activities, including employment. We encourage women, minorities and differently abled persons to apply for employment positions of interest. Open Date 08/18/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: Date of Birth Social Security Number Gender Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. Quick Link https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52246 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley UT System Employee Benefits UT System Fraud Reporting State of Texas Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal Where the money goes To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
