      "description": "The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley Job Site | Graduate Assistant - Graduate Recruitment Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Office Location The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley 1201 W. University Drive Human Resources MASS Building 2 nd Floor Edinburg, TX  78539 Edinburg: (956)665-2451 Brownsville: (956) 882-8205 Office hours: Monday-Friday 8:00a.m. - 5:00p.m. Staff Recruitment: careers@utrgv.edu School of Medicine Recruitment: SOMCareers@utrgv.edu Graduate Assistantships: assistantships@utrgv.edu Faculty Recruitment: College of Engineering & Computer Science: cecs@utrgv.edu Robert C. Vackar College of Business & Entrepreneurship: cobe@utrgv.edu College of Sciences Office of the Dean: cos@utrgv.edu College of Education and P-16 Integration: cep@utrgv.edu College of Fine Arts: cofa@utrgv.edu College of Liberal Arts: liberalarts@utrgv.edu Website: https://careers.utrgv.edu Graduate Assistant - Graduate Recruitment Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: *Date of Birth *Social Security Number *Gender *Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. Posting Details Title Information Assistantship Title Graduate Assistant Job Class Code 10096 FLSA Exempt Minimum Qualifications 1. Currently admitted to the Graduate School 2. Be in good academic standing 3. Be registered full-time for the respective semester (nine semester credit hours during the fall semester, nine semester credit hours during spring semester, three semester credit hours during the summer session(s)), or in the required number of semester credit hours to fulfill the only remaining requirements on the degree plan. Position Information Posting Number A1345 Working Title Graduate Assistant - Graduate Recruitment Location Brownsville, Texas College N/A Department Graduate Recruitment Division Division of Strategic Enrollment and Student Affairs FTE .5 Scope of Job JOB DESCRIPTION We are seeking a highly motivated and enthusiastic Graduate Assistant to join our team and assist with our graduate recruitment efforts. As a Graduate Assistant, you will play a crucial role in attracting and advising prospective students about our graduate programs. Your primary responsibility will be to provide excellent customer service by answering inquiries and guiding prospective students through the admission process, requirements, and career outlook with a graduate degree. You will interact with prospective students via phone, email, text message, live chat, and video. DUTIES Provide exceptional customer service to prospective graduate students by promptly responding to inquiries via phone, email, text message, live chat, and video. Assist prospective students with questions regarding the admission process, requirements, deadlines, program details, and career opportunities associated with our graduate programs. Maintain a thorough knowledge and understanding of all graduate programs offered, including program prerequisites, curriculum, faculty, and any program-specific requirements. Effectively communicate the benefits and advantages of pursuing a graduate degree at UTRGV , highlighting unique features and opportunities. Coordinate and schedule appointments and information sessions for prospective students, ensuring a seamless and positive experience. Collaborate with the Graduate Recruitment team to organize and participate in recruitment events, such as graduate fairs, information sessions, and webinars. Assist in the development and enhancement of recruitment materials, including brochures, presentations, and website content. Maintain accurate records of prospective student interactions and inquiries using the appropriate customer relationship management ( CRM ) tools. Assist with other graduate recruitment duties as assigned, which may include data entry, administrative tasks, or support during recruitment campaigns. Discipline Specific Required Qualifications OTHER REQUIREMENTS Must be a full-time graduate student Strong communication skills, both verbal and written, with the ability to effectively interact with diverse individuals. Excellent customer service skills and a passion for helping others. Must be able to work independently with little supervision. Be able to work in-person on the Edinburg Campus between the hours of Monday-Friday 8:00 AM – 5:00 PM. Flexibility to work occasional evenings or weekends, as required by recruitment events. Preferred Qualifications Bilingual (English/Spanish) preferred. Customer service experience preferred. Salary Number of Vacancies 2 Desired Start Date 02/10/2025 Posting Detail Information EEO Statement It is the policy of The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley to promote and ensure equal employment opportunities for all individuals without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information or protected veteran status. In accordance with the requirements of Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, as amended, our University is committed to comply with all government requirements and ensures non-discrimination in its education programs and activities, including employment. We encourage women, minorities and differently abled persons to apply for employment positions of interest. Open Date 01/26/2026 Special Instructions to Applicants Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: Date of Birth Social Security Number Gender Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley reserves the right to discontinue accepting applications prior to the stated close date of this position, after meeting the posting requirement of three (3) calendar days. Quick Link https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/50038 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Unofficial Transcripts Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 List of 3 References The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley UT System Employee Benefits UT System Fraud Reporting State of Texas Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal Where the money goes To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
