    "https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52393": {
      "title": "ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT FOR STRATEGIC BUSINESS AFFAIRS",
      "description": "The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley Job Site | ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT FOR STRATEGIC BUSINESS AFFAIRS Skip to Main Content Home Search Jobs Job Alerts Log In /Create Account Help Office Location The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley 1201 W. University Drive Human Resources MASS Building 2 nd Floor Edinburg, TX  78539 Edinburg: (956)665-2451 Brownsville: (956) 882-8205 Office hours: Monday-Friday 8:00a.m. - 5:00p.m. Staff Recruitment: careers@utrgv.edu School of Medicine Recruitment: SOMCareers@utrgv.edu Graduate Assistantships: assistantships@utrgv.edu Faculty Recruitment: College of Engineering & Computer Science: cecs@utrgv.edu Robert C. Vackar College of Business & Entrepreneurship: cobe@utrgv.edu College of Sciences Office of the Dean: cos@utrgv.edu College of Education and P-16 Integration: cep@utrgv.edu College of Fine Arts: cofa@utrgv.edu College of Liberal Arts: liberalarts@utrgv.edu Website: https://careers.utrgv.edu ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT FOR STRATEGIC BUSINESS AFFAIRS Below you will find the details for the position including any supplementary documentation and questions you should review before applying for the opening.  To apply for the position, please click the Apply for this Job link/button. If you would like to bookmark this position for later review, click on the Bookmark link.  If you would like to print a copy of this position for your records, click on the Print Preview link. Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: *Date of Birth *Social Security Number *Gender *Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us at (956)665-8880 and/or careers@utrgv.edu. Posting Details Position Information Posting Number SRGV9124 Working Title ASSOCIATE VICE PRESIDENT FOR STRATEGIC BUSINESS AFFAIRS Number of Vacancies 1 Location Edinburg, Texas Department Finance & Business Affairs FTE 1.0 FLSA Exempt Scope of Job Reports directly to the Executive Vice President for Finance and Business Affairs and Chief Financial Officer and serves as the principal advisor on strategic business affairs, enterprise contract administration, administrative governance, and institutional business process strategy. Provides executive leadership for enterprise initiatives that strengthen operational effectiveness, standardize administrative practices, improve internal controls, and advance the University’s strategic priorities. The Associate Vice President serves as the University’s executive business owner for contract administration and leads cross-functional efforts to modernize business operations, improve service delivery, and promote operational excellence across academic and administrative divisions. The position collaborates extensively with University leadership to align business operations with institutional priorities while respecting the independent authority of other executive offices. The AVP coordinates with the Office of Legal Affairs on matters requiring legal review or legal interpretation but does not provide legal advice, establish legal positions for the University, or perform the functions of University Counsel. Description of Duties Serves as the Executive Vice President’s principal advisor on strategic business affairs, operational governance, and enterprise business strategy. Represents the Executive Vice President before institutional committees, executive workgroups, and external stakeholders as assigned. Leads high-impact institutional initiatives requiring coordination across multiple divisions. Provides executive oversight of the University’s contract administration program from intake through execution, monitoring, and records administration. Establishes administrative standards, workflows, service expectations, and performance measures for enterprise contract administration. Coordinates contract administration with Procurement and the Office of Legal Affairs while preserving each office’s independent responsibilities. Develops reporting and performance metrics that improve transparency, accountability, and customer service. Leads enterprise business process improvement and administrative modernization initiatives. Evaluates organizational workflows to improve efficiency, eliminate unnecessary complexity, strengthen internal controls, and increase scalability. Facilitates cross-functional redesign of business processes supporting institutional priorities. Develops administrative governance frameworks, business standards, and operational guidance that support consistent and effective business practices. Partners with Finance, Procurement, Human Resources, Information Technology, Facilities, Information Security, Internal Audit, and other administrative units to improve institutional effectiveness. Conducts organizational assessments and develops executive recommendations regarding operational strategy and resource utilization. Leads complex projects from planning through implementation, establishing milestones, performance indicators, and executive reporting. Exercises delegated authority from the Executive Vice President for assigned strategic initiatives and administrative business matters. Develops recommendations affecting enterprise business operations, governance, and organizational effectiveness. Negotiates operational solutions among multiple divisions to advance institutional objectives. Performs other duties as assigned. Supervision Received General supervision from assigned supervisor. Supervision Given Direct supervision of assigned staff. Required Education Bachelor’s degree from an accredited university. Preferred Education Master’s degree in Business Administration, Public Administration, Finance, or related discipline. Licenses/Certifications Preferred: Juris Doctor (J.D.) from an accredited law school. Required Experience Seven (7) years of progressively responsible senior leadership experience in higher education, government, healthcare, or another complex organization. Demonstrated success leading enterprise strategic initiatives, organizational improvement, contract administration, or business operations. Demonstrated ability to build collaborative relationships and influence organizational outcomes. Preferred Experience Experience in a public research university, academic health system, or similarly complex public institution. Experience leading enterprise operational transformation or administrative modernization initiatives. Equipment Use of standard office equipment. Working Conditions Needs to be able to successfully perform all required duties. Work is performed primarily in a general office environment. Some travel and weekend work is required. UTRGV is a distributed institution, which may require presence at multiple locations throughout the Rio Grande Valley. Other Knowledge, skills and abilities in the following areas: Enterprise contract administration, Business process strategy and redesign, Administrative governance, Strategic planning, Executive project leadership, Policy development, Operational risk assessment, Data-informed decision making, Executive communication, Relationship management. Physical Capabilities N/A Employment Category Full-Time Minimum Salary commensurate with Experience Posted Salary Commensurate with Experience Position Available Date 08/31/2026 Grant Funded Position No If Yes, Provide Grant Expiration Date Posting Detail Information EEO Statement It is the policy of The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley to promote and ensure equal employment opportunities for all individuals without regard to race, color, national origin, sex, age, religion, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information or protected veteran status. In accordance with the requirements of Title VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964, the Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972, Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and the Americans with Disabilities Act of 1990, as amended, our University is committed to comply with all government requirements and ensures non-discrimination in its education programs and activities, including employment. We encourage women, minorities and differently abled persons to apply for employment positions of interest. Special Instructions to Applicants Dear Applicant, Human Resources will not be held responsible for redacting any confidential information from the documents you attach with your application. The confidential information includes the following: Date of Birth Social Security Number Gender Ethnicity/Race Please make sure that you omit this information prior to submission. We are advising that Human Resources will be forwarding your application to the department as per your submission. If you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us at (956)665-8880 and/or careers@utrgv.edu. Additional Information UTRGV is a distributed location institution and working location is subject to change based on need. All UTRGV employees are required to have a criminal background check ( CBC ). Incomplete applications will not be considered. Substitutions to the above requirements must have prior approval from the VP of HR & Talent Development . Quick Link https://careers.utrgv.edu/postings/52391 Posting Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Are you now, or previously, employed by The University of Texas System or any of its institutions? Yes - I currently am employed by the UT System or its institutions Yes - I have previously been employed by the UT System or its institutions No - I have never been employed by the UT System or its institutions Are you a current UTRGV employee? Yes No Please select your highest level of completed education. 6th grade education 10th grade education High School Diploma or GED Associates Degree, Technical, or Trade School Degree/Certification or 60 Hours of College Hours Bachelors Degree from an accredited university Masters Degree from an accredited university Ph. D. or other terminal degree from an accredited university None of the above Please provide the field of study for your education: (Open Ended Question) Do you meet the minimum requirements for this position? Yes No Please indicate the number of years of work experience you have directly related to the position in which you are applying for: Less than 1 year 1 year 2 years 3 years 4 years 5 years 6 years 7 years 8 years 9 years 10 years Over 10 years Applicant Documents Required Documents Resume Optional Documents Cover Letter/Letter of Application Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts Reference Letter 1 Reference Letter 2 Reference Letter 3 Certifications and Licenses Training Certificates Other Document List of 3 References Unofficial Transcripts 2 Unofficial Transcripts 3 Letter of Interest Unofficial Graduate Transcripts Additional Document The University of Texas Rio Grande Valley UT System Employee Benefits UT System Fraud Reporting State of Texas Texas Homeland Security Texas Veterans Portal Where the money goes To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."
